.audit-harvest/

# Raw instrumentation traces belong in the external archive, never in the repo.
# A subagent script with an undefined path variable wrote 67 of them into
# test/observations/ss2-1v1/undefined/ on 2026-09-01 and `git add -A` committed
# them. Ignoring is the second line of defence; the first is the test in
# test/ss2-capture-attestation.test.js that fails if any are tracked.
test/observations/**/*.jsonl

# ► **EXTRACTED SS2 ASSETS ARE LOCAL-ONLY, and this is the Doom/WAD rule.**
# `AGENTS.md`: "Ship no SS2 asset... someone who clones it must still need
# their own licensed copy to play. This is about what leaves the repo, never
# about what you may build in it." So a player extracts from their OWN install
# into `assets/`, the renderer prefers them when present, and a fresh clone
# falls back to the authored vector art in `src/render/figure.js`.
#
# Ignoring is the second line of defence. The first is the test in
# test/asset-attestation.test.js, which FAILS if any extracted asset is tracked
# — exactly as test/ss2-capture-attestation.test.js does for raw traces, after
# a subagent committed 67 of those.
assets/*
!assets/README.md
